<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money rates slip on excess liquidity.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money rates slip on excess liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money rates slipped on Tuesday on excess liquidity due to an inflow of around 4.5 billion rupees of open market operation maturity, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Early in the day, the lenders were offering at 8.0 percent, but finally the deals were struck at 2.50 and 3.0 percent due to excess liquidity,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The rates on Wednesday will depend upon results of open market operation.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia 9221-5685192.</p>
